{
  "$comment": [
    "Mirrored from RaceLink_Host/racelink/domain/rf_channels.py, which stays the source of truth.",
    "Vendored here because the firmware needs the table for three things the host cannot do for it:",
    "the channel dropdown in the WLED usermod settings, the info line, and the band lock.",
    "",
    "racelink_rf_channels.h is GENERATED from this file by scripts/generate_rf_channels.py;",
    "tests/test_rf_channels.py regenerates and compares, so the header cannot drift from the table.",
    "The release publishes this file verbatim as `rf_channels` in the assets.json sidecar, which is",
    "how the web flasher offers exactly the channels the selected firmware version understands.",
    "",
    "There is deliberately no 433 MHz region: the host does not define one, and",
    "RfConfigNvs::validate() rejects anything outside 863-928 MHz."
  ],
